<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mamercus Aemilius Mamercinus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 437–426 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mamercus Aemilius Mamercinus was a Roman statesman who was appointed dictator three times, in 437, 434 and 426 BCE. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy</a>, as dictator in 434 BCE he limited the term of the censors to eighteen months, and in 426 BCE he defeated Veii and Fidenae and captured and destroyed Fidenae, whose land then passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p></div>
